    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Atlassian describes itself as a maker of collaboration software for software, IT and business teams. Its site says products such as Jira, Confluence and Trello help teams organize, discuss and complete shared work, and it presents Jira, Confluence, Loom and Rovo AI agents as one connected platform for planning, tracking and delivering work. The company was founded in 2002 and is headquartered in Sydney, Australia.\n\nIts AI offerings include Confluence AI, described as a team wiki AI with smart links and automation, and Trello AI, described as project management AI with workflow automation. Both are noted alongside Atlassian Cloud governance, and the Trello entry also notes team data exposure.\n\nAtlassian is a public company traded under the ticker TEAM, with CIK 0001650372. Its most recent revenue filing is a 10-K for the period ending 2025-06-30, reporting $5,215,304,000.",
